@startuml sequence_failure_paths
title Figure 5b - Sequence Diagram: Failure Paths of GEN-02 "Journal Exception Attribution" (hybrid) in one A6 Instance\n[Individual task · Member B]\nFailure branches F-1 to F-5 (14) modelled as nested alt fragments: a failing branch simply does not enter the computation below it,\nand every branch - failing or not - returns through the same StatePatch to A1

skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam legendFontSize 20
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign first
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #888800

participant "A1 Orchestrator\n(scheduler, mergePatch,\nDecisionSubmit)" as A1
participant "A6 FieldworkAgent\ninstance fw-L-i" as A6
participant "RuleEngine" as RE
participant "FinancialDataStore" as FDS
participant "JudgmentEngine\n(OutputValidator)" as JE
participant "LLMClient\n(main model)" as LLM
participant "A7 ReviewAgent\n(critic client)" as A7
participant "AuditTrail" as TR
participant "AuditOutputStore" as OUT
participant "ReviewQueue" as RQ
participant "A10 ConciergeAgent" as A10
actor "RCA" as RCA

autonumber

== Main line: rule stage and context assembly ==

A1 -> A6 : fanOut(layer): Send(instance fw-L-i,\nprocedures incl. GEN-02)
activate A6
A6 -> A6 : Procedure GEN-02 -> executing\nentry: new ProcedureRun(trigger = initial), loop1Rounds = 0
A6 -> RE : bindParams(rule, engagement), run(rule)\nhybrid pre-filter: the exceptions raised by the GEN-05 full journal scan
activate RE
RE -> FDS : query(sql, params)
FDS --> RE : Row[]
RE --> A6 : Exception[] with EvidencePointers\n(rule stage, no reasoning chain, no A7)
deactivate RE
A6 -> A6 : assemble the four context layers per 8.5\n(system, standards, task, data); EngagementState itself never enters the prompt

== F-3 / F-1 / F-2 / F-4: one nested alt, nothing is written outside the patch ==

alt#Gold #Cornsilk F-3b  a single batch is still over context_budget (8.5)
  A6 -> A6 : no LLM call is made; ProcedureRun -> failed,\nfailureReason = needs_manual_scope (8.5); A1 sets Procedure -> awaiting_human at fan-in
  A6 -> A6 : draft ReviewTask (kind = failed, target = ProcedureRun)\ninto the StatePatch
  A6 -> TR : log(context over budget, no LLM call made)
  note over A6, TR : **Outcome** - ProcedureRun failed (needs_manual_scope), Procedure awaiting_human,\none ReviewTask draft of kind = failed in the patch. No Judgment exists, so the\nvalidation levels and F-4 below are never entered.\nHuman narrows the scope (rerun + rerunParams) or performs it (manual_result);\nscope_limited / not_applicable also allowed (UC-04 failed row).

else within context_budget, batching included

  alt#99BBDD #EFF5FC F-3a  context_budget exceeded, batching fits
    A6 -> A6 : split into batches, never truncate; one call per batch,\none Judgment per Exception, no context shared between batches
    loop for each batch: batchNo on ProcedureRun
      A6 -> LLM : complete(prompt_batch, output_schema)
      A6 -> TR : log(llm_call: model version, prompt, input hash, params, batchNo)
    end
    note over A6, TR : Evidence coverage (8.4) is computed per batch; cross-batch aggregation\nis done by rules, not by the LLM. Everything below is drawn for one call\nand applies to every batch.
  else the context fits in a single call
    A6 -> LLM : complete(prompt, output_schema)
    A6 -> TR : log(llm_call: model version, prompt, input hash, params)
  end

  alt#99BBDD #EFF5FC F-1  LLM endpoint times out or is rate limited (14)
    LLM --> A6 : timeout / 429 rate limited
    A6 -> TR : log(attempt no., failure reason)
    A6 -> A6 : retry with backoff **inside the node** (18.5);\nstill failing -> the call is queued for a later window (14)
    A6 -> A6 : window exhausted -> engine fallback (8.6): **hybrid** degrades to the rule engine\nand keeps the rule result, Exception.disposition = unattributed; engine = **llm** has no rule\nresult to fall back on -> ProcedureRun -> failed, failureReason = llm_unavailable
    A6 -> A6 : draft ReviewTask (kind = unattributed, target = Exception)\ninto the StatePatch; kind = failed, target = ProcedureRun when engine = llm
    note over A6, TR : **Outcome** - Procedure awaiting_human, no Judgment either way,\nso validation and F-4 are never entered.\nhybrid: rule result kept, Exception unattributed, ReviewTask draft kind = unattributed;\nallowed decisions override / misstatement / more_procedures (UC-04), confirm is refused,\nan unattributed exception is not a disposition.\nengine = llm: ProcedureRun failed (llm_unavailable), ReviewTask draft kind = failed;\nallowed decisions rerun / manual_result / scope_limited / not_applicable.

  else response received
    LLM --> A6 : structured output (candidate explanations + reasoning chains)
    A6 -> JE : buildJudgment(findings, GEN-02)
    activate JE

    alt#7FA87F #F2F8F2 F-2a  syntax or structure violates output_schema, 2 retries exhausted (8.6 levels 1-2)
      JE -> JE : validateSyntax, validateStructure -> fail
      loop at most 2 retries, parse error handed back
        JE --> A6 : validation error
        A6 -> LLM : complete(prompt + error, output_schema)
        A6 -> TR : log(retry attempt and its failure)
      end
      JE --> A6 : retries exhausted, no valid Judgment object
      deactivate JE
      A6 -> A6 : engine fallback (8.6): **hybrid** keeps the rule result,\nException.disposition = unattributed; for engine = **llm** the same\nexhaustion sets ProcedureRun -> failed instead
      A6 -> A6 : draft ReviewTask (kind = unattributed, target = Exception)\ninto the StatePatch; kind = failed, target = ProcedureRun when engine = llm
      A6 -> TR : log(validation exhausted, fallback taken)
      note over A6, TR : **Outcome** - Procedure awaiting_human; hybrid: rule result kept,\nException unattributed, ReviewTask draft kind = unattributed.\nengine = llm: ProcedureRun failed, ReviewTask draft kind = failed.\nNo Judgment exists, so F-4 is never entered.

    else levels 1-2 pass, a Judgment object exists

      alt#99BBDD #EFF5FC F-2b  reference validation fails (8.6 level 3)
        JE -> JE : validateReferences: sourceId exists, amount matches the entry,\ndocument type matches evidence_required
        alt some pointers are still valid
          JE --> A6 : that step flagged unsupported and **kept** (8.3);\nJudgment continues with reduced evidence coverage
          note over A6, JE : **Outcome** - Judgment kept with unsupported steps,\nno ReviewTask draft of its own; it continues into F-4 below.
        else no valid pointer at all
          JE --> A6 : Judgment kept whole, nothing discarded;\nthe whole Judgment is degraded to the human queue (7.4)
          A6 -> A6 : draft ReviewTask (kind = normal, target = Judgment)\ninto the StatePatch
          note over A6, JE : **Outcome** - Judgment kept, Procedure awaiting_human,\nReviewTask draft kind = normal; it still passes through F-4 below.
        end

      else F-2c  semantic validation fails (8.6 level 4)
        JE -> JE : validateSemantics: reasoning chain non-empty, every fact carries a pointer,\nevery inference cites a previous step, confidence within 0..1,\nsuggested action agrees with the conclusion
        JE --> A6 : Judgment **kept**, degraded per 7.4 - nothing discarded
        A6 -> A6 : draft ReviewTask (kind = normal, target = Judgment)\ninto the StatePatch
        note over A6, JE : **Outcome** - Judgment kept and flagged, Procedure awaiting_human,\nReviewTask draft kind = normal. Whether the evidence supports the\nconclusion is re-derived by A7 under GEN-09 (8.6 level 4).

      else all four levels pass
        JE --> A6 : Judgment (conclusion, reasoning chain,\ncounter-argument, confidence)
      end
      deactivate JE

      alt#Gold #Cornsilk F-4  GEN-09 trigger hit on this Judgment and A7 still inconsistent after Loop 1 (11, UC-03)
        A6 -> A7 : independentConclusion(evidence pointers), compare(own, theirs)\n**the only direct agent-to-agent call**: in = pointers + conclusion, out = criticVerdict + independent conclusion and reasoning chain
        activate A7
        A7 --> A6 : criticVerdict = inconsistent,\ncriticReasonType = insufficient_evidence
        deactivate A7
        loop Loop 1: loop1Rounds < 3 and new system-internal evidence found
          A6 -> A6 : gatherMore() -> new ProcedureRun(trigger = loop1_retry),\nre-generate, re-validate (8.6), A7 re-compares; old Judgment -> supersededBy
        end
        A6 -> A6 : final Judgment flagged dispute, disputeRounds recorded;\nA6 conclusion and A7 independent conclusion kept side by side with both chains
        A6 -> A6 : draft ReviewTask (kind = dispute, target = Judgment)\ninto the StatePatch -> adjudication lane, no confidence ranking, no blind
        note over A6, A7 : **Outcome** - last ProcedureRun succeeded; A1 sets Procedure -> in_dispute at fan-in\n(not a settled state, blocks FIN-05), ReviewTask draft kind = dispute.\nOnly decision allowed: dispute_resolution = a6_upheld / a7_upheld / neither\n(neither must carry human_conclusion or more_procedures).

      else GEN-09 not hit, or the verdict is consistent
        A6 -> A6 : criticVerdict = skipped or consistent
        note over A6, A7 : **Outcome** - no dispute; the effective level from the common step below\ndecides the landing: L1 / L2 / blind / 9.1 mandatory rows draft a ReviewTask\nkind = normal; L3 normal items and L4 are auto-closed by A1 at fan-in (Procedure -> completed)\n(9.2 still samples 5% as kind = blind). Runs, Judgments and task drafts stay in the patch.
      end

      A6 -> A6 : apply 7.4 downgrade rules and compute confidence (8.4) for every kept\nJudgment (dispute, unsupported, downgraded or clean)
    end
  end
end

== F-5  Fan-in: one return path for every branch above (8.6 agent layer, 14) ==

note over A6, A1 : Failure results travel back exactly like successful ones: the instance writes\nnothing to AuditOutputStore or ReviewQueue itself (18.4). Everything above is\na draft until A1 has merged it; business results reach AuditOutputStore only\nthrough A1, after the merge has passed.

alt#Gold #Cornsilk F-5a  the instance returned a StatePatch
  A6 --> A1 : StatePatch (Judgments, Exceptions, ProcedureRuns, ReviewTask drafts)
  A1 -> A1 : mergePatch: four checks (8.6 agent layer) - write scope (18.3.1),\ntype, ID uniqueness, foreign key (Judgment -> procedure_pack)

  alt#99BBDD #EFF5FC any check fails, first attempt
    A1 -> TR : log(merge rejected, failing check, patch **not** merged)
    A1 -> A6 : re-run this execution once (new ProcedureRun)
    A6 --> A1 : StatePatch (re-run)
    A1 -> A1 : the same four checks again

    alt#7FA87F #F2F8F2 the re-run patch fails again
      A1 -> A1 : every ProcedureRun in the patch -> failed, failureReason = patch_rejected;\nthe drafts both patches carried are discarded with them
      A1 -> OUT : write(failed ProcedureRuns)
      A1 -> RQ : publish(one ReviewTask kind = failed per ProcedureRun)
      note over A1, RQ : **Outcome** - Procedure awaiting_human. This is the only case in which A1 creates a\nReviewTask itself (the system failed to execute it); everywhere else A6 drafts the task\nand A1 only publishes it.\nAllowed decisions: rerun / manual_result / scope_limited / not_applicable (UC-04).

    else the re-run patch passes the four checks
      A1 -> A1 : merge by ID into EngagementState\n(reducer keeps the highest version)
      A1 -> OUT : write(Judgments, Exceptions, ProcedureRuns)
      A1 -> RQ : publish(ReviewTask drafts from the re-run patch)
      note over A1, RQ : **Outcome** - the same landing as a first-attempt pass: one extra ProcedureRun\nfor the re-run, nothing failed. Business Store first, checkpoint after (18.5).
    end

  else all four checks pass on the first patch
    A1 -> A1 : merge by ID into EngagementState\n(reducer keeps the highest version)
    A1 -> OUT : write(Judgments, Exceptions, ProcedureRuns)
    A1 -> RQ : publish(ReviewTask drafts from the patch)
    note over A1, RQ : The drafts become visible to the human only at this point. A task the user can\nsee is therefore always a task whose state A1 has already accepted.
  end

else F-5b  the instance crashed or timed out, no StatePatch at all
  A1 -> A1 : nothing returns from fw-L-i: re-schedule its remaining procedures to other\ninstances (grouping is an optimisation, not a constraint); Judgments already\nmerged from its earlier patches are kept
  A1 -> TR : log(schedule change; the schedule table is deterministic, no LLM)
  note over A1, TR : **Outcome** - no ReviewTask at all and nothing written for this execution;\nthe remaining procedures stay planned and re-enter executing under another\ninstance with a new ProcedureRun. The human is never notified.
end
deactivate A6

== Main line: every branch that needs a human ends in the same queue (details in Figure 4a) ==

opt a published ReviewTask exists for this procedure
  note over RQ, RCA : Entered only for tasks the merge actually published. Results that closed\nautomatically and were not sampled (9.2), and the silent re-scheduling of F-5b,\npublish no task and expect no human decision.
  A10 -> RQ : rank()
  RQ --> A10 : next ReviewTask by 9.1 tier
  activate A10
  A10 -> RCA : present(task) with the decisions allowed for its kind:\nreasoning chain and evidence, or rule result (unattributed),\nor failure reason (failed), or scope request (scope_limited)
  RCA -> A10 : decision + reason (empty reason refused)
  A10 -> A1 : submit(ReviewRecord) via DecisionSubmit -\nwhole object built verbatim from the form fields, no LLM
  deactivate A10
  A1 -> A1 : validate targetVersion, gate state and\ntask kind x decision matrix (UC-04)
  A1 -> OUT : write(ReviewRecord), recompute Procedure status: completed only when every\nReviewTask is decided, no open dispute, no follow-up run pending and the period is covered\n(timing != interim or periodCovered); otherwise awaiting_human / in_dispute / executing / interim_completed
  A1 -> TR : log(human decision, reviewer, dwell time)
end

legend right
  |= Fragment |= Failure (14) |= Outcome left in the StatePatch |
  | F-1 | LLM timeout or rate limit | hybrid: rule result kept, Exception unattributed, draft kind unattributed; engine = llm: ProcedureRun failed (llm_unavailable), draft kind failed; Procedure awaiting_human |
  | F-2a | output_schema violated, 2 retries exhausted | same engine fallback as F-1 (hybrid unattributed, llm failed) |
  | F-2b | EvidencePointer references invalid | some valid: step flagged unsupported and kept, Judgment continues; none valid: Judgment kept, draft kind normal |
  | F-2c | semantic validation fails (chain, pointers, confidence, action) | Judgment kept and degraded per 7.4, draft kind normal, Procedure awaiting_human |
  | F-3 | context_budget exceeded | batched calls with batchNo; a single batch still over -> ProcedureRun failed (needs_manual_scope), draft kind failed |
  | F-4 | Loop 1 exhausted, A7 inconsistent | Judgment flagged dispute, draft kind dispute, Procedure in_dispute |
  | F-5 | merge checks fail, or no patch returns at all | patch received: checks, one re-run, then pass (merge, write, publish) or fail (runs failed, A1 publishes failed tasks); no patch: silent re-scheduling |
  ----
  Notation: **Outcome** states what a branch leaves behind - ProcedureRun, Procedure and the kind of any ReviewTask draft.
  It is not a stop: failure results still travel back to A1 in the StatePatch, and the nesting of the alt fragments is what
  keeps a failed branch out of the validation, F-4 and confidence steps below it. ReviewTasks become visible to the human
  only after A1 has merged the patch (18.4): A6 drafts them, A1 publishes them, and a patch rejected twice publishes none
  of its drafts - only the failed tasks A1 creates itself. Business results (Judgments, Exceptions, ProcedureRuns) are
  written to AuditOutputStore by A1 after the merge, never by the instance or the JudgmentEngine.
  The opt at the bottom marks the human lane as conditional: it is entered only for a task the merge published, so an
  automatic close that was not sampled and a silent re-scheduling (F-5b) end the execution without any human step.
  Every LLM call, retry and failure writes one AuditTrail line (M-07); retry, degradation and timeout are
  implemented inside the node, not left to framework defaults (18.5).
  A1, A5 and A9 never call the LLM. A6 -> A7 is the only direct agent-to-agent call; every other exchange
  travels as a StatePatch through A1. The human talks only to A10, and A10 writes only through DecisionSubmit.
endlegend
@enduml
